  "notes": "The one lane on the roster that lives in a major key — four-chord pop motion, vi–IV–I–V and its rotations, under a pop-trap grid that keeps getting cut up. Tempo is deliberately unstable across 95–180 because the volatility is the genre: 16th hats, a hard 2-and-4 with a clap on it, and fills that are 32nds and 64ths with a stuttered off-snare landing where the edit was. Bright supersaws sit high and the topline arcs across the whole four bars instead of looping a riff.",
